🚀 Day 5 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 75 – Sort Colors.

This problem helped me understand the Dutch National Flag Algorithm, an elegant in-place sorting technique that sorts an array containing only 0s, 1s, and 2s in a single traversal.

💡 Approach: Dutch National Flag Algorithm (Three Pointers)

I used three pointers:

low → points to the position where the next 0 should be placed.
mid → traverses the array.
high → points to the position where the next 2 should be placed.

As I traversed the array:

If the current element was 0, I swapped it with the low pointer and moved both low and mid.
If it was 1, I simply moved mid.
If it was 2, I swapped it with the high pointer and decreased high without moving mid, since the swapped element still needed to be processed.

This allowed the array to be sorted in one pass with O(n) time and O(1) extra space.

